I imagine it&#x27;s (implicitly?) referring to avoiding whole-of-program analysis.<p>For example, given a declaration<p><pre><code>  int* func(int* a);
</code></pre>
What&#x27;s the relationship between the return value and the input? You can&#x27;t know without diving into &#x27;func&#x27; itself; they could be the same pointer or it could return a freshly allocated pointer, without getting into the even more esoteric options.<p>Trying to solve this without recursively analysing a whole program at once is infeasible.<p>Rust&#x27;s approach was to require more information to be provided by function definitions, but that&#x27;s new syntax, and not backwards compatible, so not a palatable option for C++.
